# JavaScript Arrays 📚

An array is an ordered list of values indexed by integers starting at `0`:

```javascript
const colors = ["red", "green", "blue"];

console.log("First color:", colors[0]);
console.log("Length:", colors.length);

// Mutating methods
colors.push("purple"); // Adds to end
colors.pop();          // Removes from end
colors.unshift("cyan");// Adds to beginning
colors.shift();        // Removes from beginning

console.log("Final colors:", colors);
```

