# The Power of `.reduce()` 🧺

`.reduce()` executes a reducer callback over the array to compute a **single cumulative value** (sum, average, group, or object):

```javascript
const prices = [10, 25, 40, 15];

// reduce((accumulator, currentValue) => ..., initialValue)
const totalPrice = prices.reduce((sum, price) => sum + price, 0);

console.log("Total Price: $" + totalPrice);
```

<!-- FULL_CODE_START
const prices = [10, 25, 40, 15];
const totalPrice = prices.reduce((sum, price) => sum + price, 0);
console.log("Total Price: $" + totalPrice);

// Counting word frequency with reduce
const fruits = ["apple", "banana", "apple", "orange", "banana", "apple"];
const counts = fruits.reduce((acc, fruit) => {
  acc[fruit] = (acc[fruit] || 0) + 1;
  return acc;
}, {});
console.log("Fruit tally:", counts);
