# Searching Arrays 🔎

Modern search methods:

```javascript
const users = [
  { id: 1, name: "Sarah", role: "admin" },
  { id: 2, name: "David", role: "user" }
];

// 1. find(): Returns first matching element (or undefined)
const admin = users.find(u => u.role === "admin");
console.log("Found Admin:", admin.name);

// 2. includes(): Boolean check for primitive value
const tags = ["tech", "coding", "web"];
console.log("Has coding tag?", tags.includes("coding"));

// 3. some() & every()
console.log("Any user is admin?", users.some(u => u.role === "admin")); // true
console.log("All users are admin?", users.every(u => u.role === "admin")); // false
```

