# Object Utility Methods 🛠️

Extract keys, values, or key-value entries from plain objects:

```javascript
const hero = { name: "Batman", city: "Gotham", allies: 3 };

console.log(Object.keys(hero));   // ["name", "city", "allies"]
console.log(Object.values(hero)); // ["Batman", "Gotham", 3]
console.log(Object.entries(hero));// [["name", "Batman"], ["city", "Gotham"], ...]

// Clean iteration with Object.entries:
for (const [key, val] of Object.entries(hero)) {
  console.log(`${key} -> ${val}`);
}
```

