# Slicing vs Splicing Arrays ✂️

- **`.slice(start, end)` (Immutable):** Returns a shallow copy slice without modifying original.
- **`.splice(start, count, ...items)` (Mutable):** Modifies the array in place!

```javascript
const letters = ["A", "B", "C", "D", "E"];

// Slice creates copy from index 1 up to index 3 (exclusive)
const sub = letters.slice(1, 3);
console.log("Sub slice:", sub); // ["B", "C"]
console.log("Original untouched:", letters);

// Splice removes 2 elements starting at index 2 and replaces them
letters.splice(2, 2, "X", "Y");
console.log("After splice mutation:", letters); // ["A", "B", "X", "Y", "E"]
```

